exports[`goldens de DOM — Code review (VIEW.creview) > creview de ficheiro Rust com múltiplos achados (clone/unwrap/LIMIT) 1`] = `
"<div class="page" style="max-width:860px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px"><div class="score bad">38<small>/100</small></div><div><h1 style="margin:0">Code review</h1><div class="sub notr" style="margin:0">svc/load.rs</div></div><span style="flex:1"></span><button class="mini">Open file</button></div>
   <div class="sub" style="margin-top:12px">Rule-based checks for correctness, security, performance and the project rules. They point at evidence; you decide what to change.</div>
   <div class="rv"><div class="rv-h"><span class="tag" style="color:var(--red);border-color:var(--red)">bug</span><b>Loop iterates over a clone of the iterator</b><span class="sp"></span><button class="lnk">line 3</button></div><div class="rv-b"><p>The original iterator never advances, so any check after the loop (like <code>peek()</code>) sees stale state.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Use <code>.by_ref()</code> to keep one cursor.</p></div></div><div class="rv"><div class="rv-h"><span class="tag" style="color:var(--red);border-color:var(--red)">bug</span><b>LIMIT without ORDER BY</b><span class="sp"></span><button class="lnk">line 4</button></div><div class="rv-b"><p>SQLite returns rows in whatever order is cheapest; “recent” lists become arbitrary.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Add <code>ORDER BY created_at DESC</code> and an index on (filter, order) columns.</p></div></div><div class="rv"><div class="rv-h"><span class="tag" style="color:var(--yellow);border-color:var(--yellow)">risk</span><b>unwrap() on a fallible value</b><span class="sp"></span><button class="lnk">line 2</button></div><div class="rv-b"><p>Panics on bad input and takes the whole service down.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Return a typed error with <code>?</code> or map it.</p></div></div></div>"
`;

